{
  "_readme": [
    "THE LANE MAP (ADR 095). One register naming each CI lane and the paths that make it run.",
    "tooling/ci/lane-detect.mjs --lane <name> is the `detect` job of each lane's callee workflow",
    "(.github/workflows/lane-<name>.yml): it answers affected=true on a push to main, on any event that",
    "is not a pull_request, on a changed path this map does not name at all, and whenever the diff",
    "cannot be read; otherwise affected is true only when a changed path matches that lane's globs.",
    "tooling/ci/lane-verdict.mjs is each callee's always-run tail job, and the only licence it gives a",
    "skipped work job is detect's affected=false.",
    "`unclaimed` names paths no lane grades beyond the guards that always run: a change touching only",
    "these runs no lane. A path matching NEITHER a lane nor `unclaimed` is unmapped, and an unmapped",
    "path runs every lane: the map failing open is the safe direction.",
    "A lane's globs name everything its jobs READ, not only the directory they build: the Worker",
    "tests read every workflow file, the ops register and one Dart source, so those are workers paths.",
    "`lane-detect.mjs --check` (guard-meta) fails on a tracked file no entry claims and on a glob that",
    "matches no tracked file. Glob syntax: `**` spans directories, `*` stays inside one path segment.",
    "A lane's `callee`, when present, is the workflow whose detect job runs `lane-detect.mjs --lane",
    "<name>`, and --check fails when that file is missing or names another lane.",
    "Only `workers` has a callee today (extensions-ci.yml keeps its own discover job until it adopts",
    "lane-detect); the other lanes' globs are written now so that `unmapped` means new to the map,",
    "not a lane that has not moved yet (O-CI-LANES-NOT-CALLABLE-UNITS).",
    "deployUnits: for each production deploy unit, the repo paths whose change makes a new publish of that unit worth doing. Keyed by the ledger environment tooling/ci/record-deployment.mjs writes the unit's Deployment under; the key \"<app>-web\" stands for every app in deploy-web.yml's matrix (subscriptiontracker-web, and each app after it).",
    "Read by tooling/ci/plan-deploy.mjs before every publish: it diffs the unit's latest SUCCESSFUL Deployment against the target commit and publishes only when a changed path matches one of these globs (row O-DEPLOY-IS-NOT-ONE-GATED-LANE, limb 3).",
    "Since ADR 095 §4 (2026-09-25) the deploy workflows carry no push paths and no dorny filters: they run only as ci.yml's deploy-web and deploy-workers call jobs, after ci-gate, and these globs alone decide what publishes. The copies went with the triggers, and so did tooling/ci/test/deploy-units.test.mjs's equality checks; that test now holds the units' own shape, and fails when either deploy workflow grows a trigger back.",
    "Glob shapes: `X/**` (a tree), `X/*.ext` or `X/*` (files directly in X), or a literal path. plan-deploy.mjs refuses any other shape rather than guessing, through globClaims in tooling/ci/deploy-globs.mjs (moved there from assert-deploy-triggers-deploy.mjs on 2026-09-26, so the plan imports no guard).",
    "\"nikatru-site\" (2026-09-25, row O-APEX-SITE-DEPLOYS-OUTSIDE-THE-PIPELINE, D3a) is the apex site sites/nikatru, published by deploy-web.yml's `site` job to the Direct Upload Pages project nikatru-apex: the site, the generator and registry it rebuilds the discovery surface from, the import closure of every script that job runs, and the workflow itself.",
    "\"nikatru-site\" claims tooling/ci/deploy-globs.mjs, not assert-deploy-triggers-deploy.mjs (2026-09-26, E-a2), exactly as \"<app>-web\" does: plan-deploy.mjs takes globClaims from there, and that guard now imports tooling/ci/worker-set.mjs and the platform register, which would otherwise join this unit's import closure and republish the apex site on every register edit."
  ],
